WEBVTT

00:09:29.313 --> 00:09:30.489
There was a theory.

00:09:30.513 --> 00:09:32.924
It was due to a Russian
mathematical physicist.

00:09:32.948 --> 00:09:34.358
It was a complicated theory;

00:09:34.382 --> 00:09:36.493
I'll tell you what it was soon enough.

00:09:36.517 --> 00:09:38.365
It was a terribly complicated theory,

00:09:38.389 --> 00:09:41.226
full of very difficult
integrals and formulas

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:43.075
and mathematics and so forth.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.837
And it sort of worked,
but it didn't work very well.

00:09:46.861 --> 00:09:48.203
The only way it worked

00:09:48.227 --> 00:09:51.446
is when the helium atoms
were very, very far apart.

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:54.183
And unfortunately,

00:09:54.207 --> 00:09:57.365
the helium atoms in liquid helium
are right on top of each other.

00:09:57.389 --> 00:10:00.730
Feynman decided, as a sort
of amateur helium physicist,